    use checkForZero(int b) to make further test for proper input on
    division and modulo cases

Author: Eric Clothier <eric.clothier@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Feb 11 21:24:57 2025 -0500

    add error checking on <std::>cin extractions

    add two functions, ignoreLine() and clearFailedExtraction()
    ignoreLine():
        clears any extraneous input after extracting from
        <std::>cin - i.e. user entered "6 8 7" when prompted
        for a single integer
    clearFailedExtraction():
        checks for an extraction failure and, if found, clears
        fail mode from <std::>cin, and clears input buffer using
        ignoreLine(); terminates program immediately on entry of
        'EOF' character; returns <true> if extraction failed,
        <false> for extraction success

    test extraction status after menu selection input, prompt for
    retry on failure

    test for extraction failure after all operand inputs, prompt
    for retyr on failure

